### 7. Runtime `ExpressionSet.Compile` Crash Investigation & Resolution - Completed
* **Incident Description**:
  - During live testing of [`[A - Quest] EK 12-58 [Kick].xml`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Default%20Profiles/1-90%20Questing%20Profile%20Pack/Classic/%5BA%20-%20Quest%5D%201-58%20%5BKick%5D/%5BA%20-%20Quest%5D%20EK%2012-58%20%5BKick%5D.xml), the bot stopped abruptly at line 3777 with:
    ```
    Compiling expression '!IsQuestCompleted(26761)' @ line 3777
    Unable to evaluate/compile condition in If tag. Please check your profile.
    Honorbuddy stopped
    System.ArgumentOutOfRangeException: Index was out of range. Must be non-negative and less than the size of the collection.
    Parameter name: index
       at Styx.CommonBot.Profiles.Quest.Order.ExpressionSet.Compile(ExpressionError[]& errors)
       at Styx.CommonBot.Profiles.Quest.Order.ConditionHelper.Class716.smethod_0(String string_1, Nullable`1 nullable_1)
       at Styx.CommonBot.Profiles.Quest.Order.ConditionHelper.Class716.method_0()
       at Bots.Quest.QuestOrder.ForcedIf.OnStart()
    ```
* **Root Cause Reverse Engineering**:
  1. **Condition Evaluation Architecture**:
     - Honorbuddy contains a fast-path regex evaluator (`Class601`) that matches 6 specific composite patterns (`HasQuest && IsQuestCompleted`, `HasQuest && !IsQuestCompleted`, `!HasQuest && IsQuestCompleted`, `!HasQuest && !IsQuestCompleted`, `HasQuest`, and `!HasQuest`).
     - Condition expressions outside these 6 patterns (such as `!IsQuestCompleted(26761)`) return `null` from `Class601.smethod_0`, forcing the engine to compile a dynamic lambda via `ExpressionSet.Compile`.
  2. **The AppDomain Assembly Reference Leak**:
     - Inside `ExpressionSet.Compile`, Honorbuddy enumerates all loaded assemblies in the AppDomain:
       ```csharp
       foreach (var asm in AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies())
           if (!asm.IsDynamic && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(asm.Location))
               cp.ReferencedAssemblies.Add(asm.Location);
       ```
     - Prior builds of `Bots/AutoAngler2/AutoAngler2.csproj` lacked `<Private>False</Private>` on references to `Honorbuddy`, `Tripper.Tools`, and transitive assemblies.
     - As a result, MSBuild copied duplicate versions of `Newtonsoft.Json.dll`, `System.Data.SQLite.dll`, `Tripper.RecastManaged.dll`, and `Tripper.Tools.dll` into `Bots/AutoAngler2/bin/Debug/` and `Release/`.
     - When Honorbuddy initialized, `AssemblyLoader` scanned the subdirectories and loaded those duplicate assemblies into the AppDomain alongside the root directory assemblies.
  3. **The `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` Off-By-One Defect in Honorbuddy**:
     - When `CSharpCodeProvider.CompileAssemblyFromSource` was called, `csc.exe` produced metadata collision errors:
       `CompilerError [CS1703] Line 0, Col 0: An assembly with the same identity 'Newtonsoft.Json...' has already been imported. Try removing one of the duplicate references.`
     - Because metadata/assembly reference errors occur at **Line 0** (before any generated source code), `CompilerError.Line` (0) was smaller than `list[0].LineStart` (31).
     - In `ExpressionSet.Compile`, the error mapping loop decremented its index `num2` all the way to `-1`:
       ```csharp
       for (int num2 = list.Count - 1; num2 >= 0; num2--) {
           if (compilerError.Line >= list[num2].LineStart) break;
       }
       errors[i] = new ExpressionError(list[num2].Expression, compilerError.ErrorText);
       ```
     - Indexing `list[-1]` threw `ArgumentOutOfRangeException`, crashing the evaluation pipeline and completely swallowing the underlying CS1703 compiler error.
* **Fixes Applied**:
  1. **Purged Build Artifacts**:
     - Recursively removed all tracked and untracked `bin/` and `obj/` directories from `Bots/`, `Plugins/`, and `Routines/`, eliminating the duplicate copies of `Newtonsoft.Json.dll`, `System.Data.SQLite.dll`, `Tripper.RecastManaged.dll`, and `Tripper.Tools.dll`.
  2. **Hardened Project References**:
     - Added `<Private>False</Private>` to [`Bots/AutoAngler2/AutoAngler2.csproj`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/AutoAngler2.csproj) to prevent future builds from copying root binaries into subdirectories.
  3. **Git Hygiene & Prevention**:
     - Created root [`.gitignore`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/.gitignore) explicitly excluding `[Bb]in/`, `[Oo]bj/`, `CompiledAssemblies/`, and temporary build outputs.
* **Verification**:
  - Verified `ExpressionSet.Compile` with all AppDomain assemblies: `Compile succeeded: True` with **0 errors**.
* **Commit**: [`00ff5ef6`](https://github.com/placeholder/commit/00ff5ef6) `fix(core): remove duplicate assemblies from AutoAngler2/bin causing CS1703 compiler crash in ExpressionSet`.

